92186435627 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435629 1069 "q-132624" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435629 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435629 1071 "The time $X,$ in seconds, between two students arriving at a canteen can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.05).$ If a student has just arrived at the canteen, what is the average time until the next student arrives there?" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435629 1072 #uuid "3ab14871-8f29-5705-a194-c2697a586708" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435629 1074 "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.05).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =0.05,$ and\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{0.05}\\,\\text{sec}=20\\,\\text{sec}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next student arrives is $20$ seconds." 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435628 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435630 1069 "q-132440" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435630 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435630 1071 "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{12}),$ what is $\\text{SD}[X]?$" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435630 1072 #uuid "5e5fad29-e988-5832-87d5-889a9c3d0b32" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435630 1074 "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{5}{12}),$ we have the following standard deviation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{5}{12})} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435631 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435625 13194139534772 17592186045417 true] [17592186435631 106